  "rule_defect": {
    "affects_L9H7_verdict": false,
    "id": "D17-F3",
    "statement": "The frozen D17 rule compares RAW F against a 0.35 threshold. Applied to L11H2 it returns CONTENT_ADDRESSED at k>=175 purely from the ALiBi prior. The rule is therefore invalid for heads whose prior mass sits where the displaced band lands.",
    "why_not": "L9H7's slope is 0.0039 (near-uniform prior), so its prior on the displaced band is substantial while its measured mass there is near zero -- its excess is strongly NEGATIVE. Correcting the defect strengthens INDEX_ADDRESSED rather than weakening it."
  },
